<main class="site-main col-xs-12 col-sm-8 left-block" id="main">
<article class="post hentry">
<a href="/en/blog-details.html">
</a>
<header class="entry-header">
</header>
<div class="entry-content">
<div class="entry-content">
<div class="post-frame">
<img alt="Post image" src="/images/ccrs.jpg"/>
<div class="img-ref">Nguồn: kinhtexanh.vn</div>
</div>
<h3>Introductory Article:</h3>
<h4>• Value:</h4>
<p>
    The Rừng Sác Base holds exceptional historical, ecological, and educational value. This vast mangrove forest area was recognized by UNESCO as a World Biosphere Reserve in 2000. At the same time, Rừng Sác served as an important revolutionary base during the resistance war against the United States and was designated a National Historical Site in 2004.<br/>
    The site also serves as a center for patriotic education, attracting students, youth groups, and organizations to visit and learn about national traditions. With its rich mangrove ecosystem, Rừng Sác is considered the “green lung” of southern Ho Chi Minh City.
  </p>
<div class="post-frame">
<img alt="Post image" src="/images/ccrs1.jpg"/>
<div class="img-ref">Nguồn: baochinhphu.vn</div>
</div>
<h4>• Origins:</h4>
<p>
    Rừng Sác was originally a vast mangrove forest area with rugged terrain and a dense network of rivers and canals. In 1962, the Republic of Vietnam government established the “Rừng Sác Special Zone” to control the strategic waterway route from Saigon to the sea. Later, revolutionary forces chose this area as a secret operational base.<br/>
    In 1966, the Rừng Sác Commando Unit (Detachment 10) was officially formed, operating independently, infiltrating deep into enemy territory, and fighting right in the heart of the opposition’s stronghold.
  </p>
<div class="post-frame">
<img alt="Post image" src="/images/ccrs2.jpg"/>
<div class="img-ref">Nguồn: gonatour.vn</div>
</div>
<h4>• Historical Values:</h4>
<p>
    The Rừng Sác Base was the headquarters of the 10th Commando Unit (Đoàn 10 Đặc công) — an elite and courageous force that operated deep within enemy territory. From 1966 to 1975, the unit carried out nearly 500 battles, both large and small, with notable operations such as the attack on the Victoria ship and the burning of the Nhà Bè fuel depot.<br/>
    This base played a crucial role in crippling the strategic supply lines of the U.S. and South Vietnamese forces in the South. It became a symbol of the commandos’ bravery, resilience, and willingness to endure hardship and sacrifice.
  </p>
<div class="post-frame">
<img alt="Post image" src="/images/ccrs3.jpg"/>
<div class="img-ref">Nguồn: tcdulichtphcm.vn</div>
</div>
<h4>• Structure::</h4>
<p>
    Today, the Rừng Sác Base has been developed into a National Historical Site combined with an ecological conservation area, offering visitors a vivid, immersive experience amid the mangrove forest.<br/>
The site recreates many wartime structures true to their original form — including barracks, bunkers, Hoàng Cầm kitchens, marching trails, defensive positions, bamboo spike traps, and minefields — allowing visitors to visualize the harsh yet resilient life of the Rừng Sác Commandos.<br/>
In addition, the Rừng Sác Museum features a modern architectural design that harmonizes with its natural surroundings — combining bamboo, wood, and stone with glass and steel.<br/>
Inside, the museum displays hundreds of wartime artifacts, photographs, documentaries, 3D models, and topographic maps depicting major battles.<br/>
Visitors can see firsthand various types of naval mines, guns, weapons, and commando equipment once used in the war zone, creating a lively and authentic historical experience.<br/>
The museum also holds commemorative ceremonies honoring the 915 Rừng Sác Commandos who fell in nearly a decade of combat.<br/>
Beyond its historical value, the base preserves the pristine beauty of the mangrove ecosystem, forming a unique combination of ecological tourism and patriotic education.<br/>
The site regularly welcomes youth groups, students, and organizations for “Back-to-the-Roots” programs, where participants can spend a day as soldiers, paddle canoes, hang hammocks in the forest, and listen to wartime stories.<br/>
Thus, Rừng Sác is not only a historical monument, but also a cultural and educational space, symbolizing patriotism, resilience, and the deep connection between people, nature, and history.
  </p>
<div class="post-frame">
<img alt="Post image" src="/images/ccrs4.jpg"/>
<div class="img-ref">Nguồn: hanoimoi.vn</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
